# Dev + production refresh (AUTOMANQANEBI.GE)

## After every completed task (local)

**სავალდებულო:** ყოველი დავალების დასრულების შემდეგ **აუცილებლად განაახლე ტერმინალი** (`npm run dev`) — ნუ დაელოდები მოთხოვნას.

Restart after finished tasks that change app code, config, deps, locales, etc.

```powershell
Get-NetTCPConnection -LocalPort 3000,3001,3002 -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue | ForEach-Object { Stop-Process -Id $_.OwningProcess -Force -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue }; Start-Sleep -Seconds 1; cd "C:\Users\hp\Desktop\AUTOMANQANEBI.GE"; npm run dev
```

Wait for `Ready`. Skip only for pure Q&A with zero file changes.

## Shortcut: user message `1` → production (automanqanebi.ge)

If the user message is exactly **`1`** (or clearly means only “განაახლე საიტი / refresh production”):

1. **Deploy production** to Firebase so **https://automanqanebi.ge** updates:

```powershell
cd "C:\Users\hp\Desktop\AUTOMANQANEBI.GE"; npx -y firebase-tools@latest deploy --only hosting,functions,firestore,storage --project automanqanebi1
```

(Do **not** include `apphosting` in the default `1` deploy — it previously failed with a JSON/XML upload error. Hosting+functions is what serves the live site.)

2. Also restart the local `npm run dev` terminal (same PowerShell as above) and wait for `Ready`.
3. Reply briefly with deploy result + production URL: https://automanqanebi.ge  
4. No other work unless they asked for more in the same message.

If deploy fails (auth, Blaze plan, network), tell the user the error clearly and the next step (e.g. `npx firebase login`).

## Behavior

- Local restart is part of task completion; confirm `Ready`
- Do not ask “should I restart/deploy?” — do it when the rules say so
